/-!
# Exterior point fusion and weak-closure transfers

The literal exterior coordinates give the two L-orbits, G₁ = C_G(z), and
the fixed point of T. The TI argument converts G₆ ≤ M into normalization
of V. Zeroth weak-closure centralization and V ≤ O₂(G₁) make ⟨Vᴳ¹⟩
elementary abelian. The constructed local Sylow choice of an L-conjugate of z′,
together with N_G(W₀) ≤ M, separates the two point orbits and constructs
the exact PointControl consumed by the terminal source argument. The
E.3.19 specialization excludes n(H) = 1 once the W₀ and C₁ bounds hold.

Zero transports the A₃ calculation through the literal LT actor and proves
the symmetry step. It derives all zeroth weak-closure bounds from r>3 and
s=3, and supplies their actual point-fusion and generation-one consumers.
First proves the original W₁ alternative and its V₆-centralization and
generation-one consumers from r>3, s=3, controlled point fusion and the
elementary point span. The L₆ actor image, radical generation and both
commutator-line exclusions are proved internally. Hall.Action constructs the
odd-prime action exclusion on the unchanged V and applies it to the actual
Borel Hall subgroup. Hall.OddNormalizer proves the specialized Chapter 4
normalizer control, and Hall combines both proofs with positive attained
E-generation to give the generation-two/Hall-three conclusion. Its Consumers
extension also discharges generation-one exclusion using the original local
geometry. Zero.Parameters proves the full-automizer
calculation r>3 and m=s=3, and applies it to the zeroth and point-control
consumers. Zero.Consumers also discharges the numerical and weak-closure
premises of the original H-star generation-one exclusion, and applies the
proved point control to the terminal commutator argument. The earlier local
and structural inputs, terminal configuration and final exterior classification
remain with their source owners.

Source assembles every clause of 12.5.6--7 and 12.5.8(2)--12 as
`exteriorFusion_of_local`. It retains only Structural1222At and the original
G₃,G₆ and point-core containments. Positive attained generation strengthens
the generation-one exclusion to n(H)>1, and the existing component escape
proof yields K₁=L₁ with normality relative to G₁. The resulting point control
is applied to the literal terminal configuration; constructing that
configuration and discharging the earlier local inputs remain with the
outer 12.5.1 source assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 12.5.6--12, printed pp.819--821.
-/
